{"path":"numeric/math/log","title":"log, logf, logl","titleHtml":"log, logf, logl","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/math/log","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"If no errors occur, the natural (base-e) logarithm of arg (ln(arg) or loge(arg)) is returned.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math\"><code>&lt;math.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; logf<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">float</span> arg <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;log<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> arg <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> logl<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> arg <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/tgmath\"><code>&lt;tgmath.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"co2\">#define log( arg )</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1-3)</span> Computes the natural (base <i>e</i>) logarithm of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> Type-generic macro: If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code> has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span></code>, <code>logl</code> is called. Otherwise, if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code> has integer type or the type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span></code>, <code>log</code> is called. Otherwise, <code>logf</code> is called. If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code> is complex or imaginary, then the macro invokes the corresponding complex function (<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/clog\"><span class=\"kw772\">clogf</span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/clog\"><span class=\"kw771\">clog</span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/clog\"><span class=\"kw773\">clogl</span></a></span></code>).</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> arg\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> floating-point value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, the natural (base-<i>e</i>) logarithm of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code> (<span class=\"texhtml\">ln(arg)</span> or <span class=\"texhtml\">log<span class=\"t-su t-su-b\">e</span>(arg)</span>) is returned.\n</p><p>If a domain error occurs, an implementation-defined value is returned (NaN where supported).\n</p><p>If a pole error occurs, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/HUGE_VAL\">-HUGE_VAL</a></span>, <code>-HUGE_VALF</code>, or <code>-HUGE_VALL</code> is returned.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Error_handling\">Error handling</h3>\n<p>Errors are reported as specified in <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/math_errhandling\"><code>math_errhandling</code></a>.\n</p><p>Domain error occurs if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code> is less than zero.\n</p><p>Pole error may occur if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code> is zero.\n</p><p>If the implementation supports IEEE floating-point arithmetic (IEC 60559),\n</p>\n<ul><li> If the argument is ±0, -∞ is returned and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_DIVBYZERO</a></span> is raised.\n</li><li> If the argument is 1, +0 is returned\n</li><li> If the argument is negative, NaN is returned and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> is raised.\n</li><li> If the argument is +∞, +∞ is returned\n</li><li> If the argument is NaN, NaN is returned.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;errno.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;fenv.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;float.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co1\">// #pragma STDC FENV_ACCESS ON</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"log(1) =&nbsp;%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, log<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"base-5 logarithm of 125 =&nbsp;%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, log<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">125</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> log<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">5</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// special values</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"log(1) =&nbsp;%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, log<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"log(+Inf) =&nbsp;%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, log<span class=\"br0\">(</span>INFINITY<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// error handling</span>\n    <span class=\"kw2\">errno</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/feclearexcept\"><span class=\"kw717\">feclearexcept</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\"><span class=\"kw728\">FE_ALL_EXCEPT</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"log(0) =&nbsp;%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, log<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">errno</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/c/error/errno_macros\"><span class=\"kw478\">ERANGE</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/c/io/perror\"><span class=\"kw878\">perror</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"    errno == ERANGE\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/fetestexcept\"><span class=\"kw718\">fetestexcept</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\"><span class=\"kw729\">FE_DIVBYZERO</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/c/io/puts\"><span class=\"kw835\">puts</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"    FE_DIVBYZERO raised\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>log(1) = 0.000000\nbase-5 logarithm of 125 = 3.000000\nlog(1) = 0.000000\nlog(+Inf) = inf\nlog(0) = -inf\n    errno == ERANGE: Numerical result out of range\n    FE_DIVBYZERO raised</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-23\">\n<ul><li> C23 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.6.7 The log functions (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.25 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> F.10.3.7 The log functions (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.6.7 The log functions (p: 178-179)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.25 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 272-273)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> F.10.3.7 The log functions (p: 380)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.6.7 The log functions (p: 244-245)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.25 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 373-375)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> F.10.3.7 The log functions (p: 522)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.6.7 The log functions (p: 225)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.22 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 335-337)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> F.9.3.7 The log functions (p: 459)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c89\">\n<ul><li> C89/C90 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1990): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 4.5.4.4 The log function \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/log10\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>log10</span><span>log10f</span><span>log10l</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes common (base-<i>10</i>) logarithm (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small \\log_{10}{x} }\">log<sub>10</sub>(x)</span>)  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/log2\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>log2</span><span>log2f</span><span>log2l</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes base-2 logarithm (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small \\log_{2}{x} }\">log<sub>2</sub>(x)</span>)  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/log1p\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>log1p</span><span>log1pf</span><span>log1pl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes natural (base-<i>e</i>) logarithm of 1 plus the given number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small \\ln{(1+x)} }\">ln(1+x)</span>)  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/exp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>exp</span><span>expf</span><span>expl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes <i>e</i> raised to the given power (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small e^x}\">e<sup>x</sup></span>)  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/clog\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>clog</span><span>clogf</span><span>clogl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes the complex natural logarithm <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>log</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Error handling","id":"Error_handling"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/math","title":"Common mathematical functions"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"log, logf, logl","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations. Computes the natural (base e) logarithm of arg."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"arg"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, the natural (base-e) logarithm of arg (ln(arg) or loge(arg)) is returned."},{"label":"Error handling","note":"Errors are reported as specified in math_errhandling."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"log10, log10f, log10l","note":"computes common (base-10) logarithm (log10(x))"},{"label":"log2, log2f, log2l","note":"computes base-2 logarithm (log2(x))"},{"label":"log1p, log1pf, log1pl","note":"computes natural (base-e) logarithm of 1 plus the given number (ln(1+x))"},{"label":"exp, expf, expl","note":"computes e raised to the given power (ex)"},{"label":"clog, clogf, clogl","note":"computes the complex natural logarithm"}]}]},"standards":["C99"],"wordCount":466,"codeBlockCount":2}
